Here is the commit message:
fixed /help bug

Here is the root cause:
In the original code, `AbstractCommand`'s constructor received a `name` parameter that could include the command name plus its argument description (e.g., "kick <player>"). The full string was used once to build `helpText` at construction time, but then the local `name` variable was truncated to just the first word (the actual command keyword) and stored in the `name` field. Later, `CommandParser.reload()` (triggered from `Server` after configuration/locale reload) called `reloadText()` on every command, which rebuilt `helpText` using the now-truncated `name` field instead of the original full name string. This caused the argument/description portion of the help text to be permanently lost after any reload, producing corrupted/incomplete `/help` output (and subclasses like `PlayerArgCommand`/`OnlinePlayerArgCommand` compounded this by re-deriving their extra hint text from the same already-truncated field). The fix removes the caching/reload mechanism entirely and instead computes help text dynamically in `getHelpText()` using an immutable `help` field that always preserves the original full name string.

Here is the patch:
 public abstract class AbstractCommand implements Command {
   protected final String name;
+  protected final String help;
   protected final String commandCode;
-  protected String helpText;
   protected CommandParser parser;

   protected AbstractCommand(String name, String commandCode) {
-    if (name != null) {
