Root cause:
In the original code, `AbstractCommand`'s constructor received a `name` parameter that could include the command name plus its argument description (e.g., "kick <player>"). The full string was used once to build `helpText` at construction time, but then the local `name` variable was truncated to just the first word (the actual command keyword) and stored in the `name` field. Later, `CommandParser.reload()` (triggered from `Server` after configuration/locale reload) called `reloadText()` on every command, which rebuilt `helpText` using the now-truncated `name` field instead of the original full name string. This caused the argument/description portion of the help text to be permanently lost after any reload, producing corrupted/incomplete `/help` output (and subclasses like `PlayerArgCommand`/`OnlinePlayerArgCommand` compounded this by re-deriving their extra hint text from the same already-truncated field). The fix removes the caching/reload mechanism entirely and instead computes help text dynamically in `getHelpText()` using an immutable `help` field that always preserves the original full name string.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
`if (splitIndex != -1) { name = name.substring(0, splitIndex); }`
`this.name = name;`
`helpText = name + Color.WHITE + " : " + t(commandCode);` (inside `reloadText()`)
Reason: The constructor truncates the local `name` variable to only the first word (the command keyword) and stores this truncated value in the `name` field, discarding the original full string (e.g., "kick <player>"). Although `helpText` is initially built correctly using the untruncated `name` before truncation, `reloadText()` later rebuilds `helpText` using the already-truncated `name` field, permanently losing the argument/description portion whenever a reload occurs.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
`help = name;`
`protected final String help;`
`return Color.DARK_GREEN + prefix + help + " : " + Color.WHITE + t(commandCode);`
Reason: The fix introduces an immutable `help` field that captures the original, untruncated name string before any truncation happens, and removes the caching/reload mechanism (`reloadText()` and `helpText` field) entirely. Instead, `getHelpText()` dynamically constructs the help text every time it's called using the preserved `help` field, ensuring the full command description (including arguments) is never lost, even after configuration or locale reloads.


